Z||000009||cadaver||08-30-2001||12:49 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Simple Fiero:<BR><B>Hey what about a corvette tranny the 6 six speed wouldn't it bolt to an LS1. What are you doing about your rear axle, there is (and call me crazy if I am wrong) no way that the fiero rear axle would handle that HP wouldn't that just snap it in half. I thought that in car & driver they made a Lingfelter Vette with a stock vette trans(not totally sure though). With over 700 hp to take on a viper.<BR>And my dad saw your msg, and said what about a buick 400, tran. Just curious that is all.<P>Thanks<BR>Craig<P>88SC, 4CYL, 5 Speed</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ok Im lost. A fiero is a transaxle. The trans and differential all in one. How are you going to put a trans from a front engine rear wheel drive car and make it work in a fiero. Oh yes I know mount the engine in the front. But that is a whole set of problems in itself.<BR>||||reg||1
