Z||000012||TONY_C||08-30-2001||10:23 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackDragon:<BR><B>cadaver: the newer corvette trans is actualy a transaxle, im not sure exactly how it works, but its something about a driveshaft from the motor to the transaxle or something of the like, like i said, not sure how it works. also for all concerned, the vw transaxle is a newer fwd trans. not sure of the vehicle.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the C5 corvette drivetrain works like this:  mounted to the engine is the torque converter (auto) or clutch and bellhousing (6 speed). connected to this is a drive shaft which rotates at engine speed to the rear end which houses the transmission and diffenential.||||reg||1
